00:42:47.630 --> 00:42:49.550
Absolutely.

00:42:49.550 --> 00:42:53.690
AUDIENCE: And the point about
measuring heat is complicated.

00:42:53.690 --> 00:42:57.712
And so you-- it's coming at
you in two different ways.

00:42:57.712 --> 00:42:59.670
And your measurement
device is vital to measure

00:42:59.670 --> 00:43:02.457
one or the other
of those ways, you

00:43:02.457 --> 00:43:04.290
might want to try a
bunch of different ways.

00:43:04.290 --> 00:43:07.470
I mean, it's-- because what
you're going to be getting is

00:43:07.470 --> 00:43:09.120
radiant heat.

00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:11.550
As bogus as this sounds,
you might actually

00:43:11.550 --> 00:43:16.290
get a more useful
measurement by [INAUDIBLE]

00:43:16.290 --> 00:43:18.870
either how hot does
it feel, or if you

00:43:18.870 --> 00:43:21.060
want to get some kind of
integrated measurement,

00:43:21.060 --> 00:43:24.282
you buy three
cantaloupes, because those

00:43:24.282 --> 00:43:25.740
are at least look
like human beings

00:43:25.740 --> 00:43:27.980
and will absorb radiated
heat about the same way.

00:43:27.980 --> 00:43:29.730
If you put them around
the thing, and then

00:43:29.730 --> 00:43:33.082
measure how hot they
get 15 minutes later.

00:43:33.082 --> 00:43:34.540
Something, but you
need an absorber

00:43:34.540 --> 00:43:36.280
that looks like a
person, [INAUDIBLE]

00:43:36.280 --> 00:43:43.090
because the metal is going to
reflect all the radiating heat.

00:43:43.090 --> 00:43:45.520
AUDIENCE: So another way to
do that is to just wrap half

00:43:45.520 --> 00:43:48.520
